    "failure_scenario": "The recent-uses list is open for Alice and the card's `name`/`slot` is changed to Bob (editor preview or a YAML edit). The new subscription delivers Bob's `event_entity_id`, `_rememberCurrentUse` adds Bob's current state to Alice's rows, and `_renderUses` parses Alice's rows under Bob's entity ID. Bob's card lists Alice's uses. A `_loadUses` still in flight for Alice also lands, because `_usesRequest` was not bumped."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/ha/services.py",
    "line": 318,
    "summary": "The `use_credential` path calls `async_fire_credential_used`/`async_log_entry` without the service call's context, so the logbook entry cannot be traced to the automation or user that reported the use.",
    "failure_scenario": "A keypad automation calls `lock_code_manager.use_credential`. The logbook entry gets a fresh Context instead of `call.context`, so its \"triggered by automation X\" cause is missing and the entry is not grouped with the automation's run. The bus event loses the same context. Thread a `context` parameter through to `async_log_entry(..., context=...)` and `hass.bus.async_fire(..., context=...)`."
  },
  {
    "file": "custom_components/lock_code_manager/model/events.py",
    "line": 81,
    "summary": "When the operation is unknown the message has no verb, so the entry reads as if the target did something.",
    "failure_scenario": "A `use_credential` call with target `cover.side_gate` always passes `CredentialOperation.UNKNOWN`. Combined with the frontend substituting the target's name, the logbook shows \"Side Gate used a PIN\", which says the gate used a PIN and names no person."
  },
  {
    "file": "ts/slot-card.ts",
    "line": 1104,
    "summary": "Every expand starts a new 30-day, attributes-included history read, even though `_useRows` is already cached and kept current by `_rememberCurrentUse`.",
    "failure_scenario": "Collapsing and expanding the row three times sends three `history/history_during_period` requests, each returning every recorded state of the event entity with full attributes for 30 days, only to show 10 rows. A busy lock means thousands of rows per read. Re-expanding should reuse the cached array and only fetch when it is undefined or null."
  },
  {
    "file": "ts/credential-uses.ts",
    "line": 576,
    "summary": "When the target has no state, the card shows its raw entity ID, while the backend's `last_used_lock` for the same use leaves the name unset.",
    "failure_scenario": "A use is reported against an entity that was removed or never existed (the PR's own `cover.side_gate` case). The \"Last used\" header shows \"Used · 3 min ago\" (websocket.py `last_used_lock` is None), but the expanded list shows \"cover.side_gate PIN\". The same card gives two different answers for the same use."
  },
  {
    "file": "ts/slot-card.ts",
    "line": 1056,
    "summary": "The \"No uses in the recorded history\" branch is effectively unreachable.",
    "failure_scenario": "After a successful load, `_rememberCurrentUse` always adds the event entity's current timestamp state, and the row is only expandable when `last_used` is set. A purged or recorder-excluded history therefore shows one use instead of the message, and the comment explaining the branch describes a state the user never sees. Either remove the branch or drop the current-state merge when the history is empty."
  },
  {
    "file": "ts/credential-uses.ts",
    "line": 515,
    "summary": "`CREDENTIAL_LABELS` copies the event_type translations from strings.json by hand, though the frontend can already render translated attribute values with `hass.formatEntityAttributeValue`.",
